Error [jet.FailureDomainNotErrorType]: Explicit failure domain `[Bad]` is not an Error type
  --> tests/ui/error_conversions/list_error_suggests_no_conversion_impl.jet:8:22
    |
  8 | check: fn(x: Int) -> Int [Bad]! {
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `!` contract may name `Err`, a Core error, a type marked `#Error`, an all-error union, or `Never`; arbitrary value types do not describe failures.
 Fix: Use a Core error, add `#Error` to a local error type, or remove the explicit error contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2417

Error [jet.MissingErrorConversion]: This implicit fallible call can't convert `[Bad]` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> tests/ui/error_conversions/list_error_suggests_no_conversion_impl.jet:14:8
    |
 14 |     _: check(1)
    |        ^^^^^
 Why: Ordinary fallible calls propagate automatically; a conversion source is one named type, so `[Bad]` has no `impl Err.From(…)`
 Fix: Handle this call locally with `??`, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402
